a python hook is available
github https://github.com/dreadwrr/pyparsec

tentative name parsec or parse c

Parse master file table written in C

Initial release and will update if spotting anything from use. if searching for new files with --cutoff
it is system time. Chose c as the job suites it perfectly. The filesize of the parser is 170kb and the
reason I made it is for my qt app that uses MFT features and needed a solution for that.

usage:

optional drive (default C:)
./parsec.exe
or
./parsec.exe S:
./parsec.exe C: --cutoff "2026-03-19 10:13:18"

dump a drive mft to file
--output <target>

note --output cannot be used with any argument below **

read from file relative or absolute
--file <mft raw>

will write to stdout csv format:
recno,sequence,parent_recno,parent_sequence,in_use,size,hard_link_count,modification_time,creation_time,mft_modified,access_time,file_attribs,type,has_ads,name,path

for a different format with timestamps and attrbs use --csv as well as --inuse can limit console writes and save time for regular mode by only listing active entries

and optional argument (one max)

search for new files by time (local system time)
--cutoff "2026-03-19 10:13:18" or 2026-03-19T10:13:18

list mft record
--target <recordno> or <frn>

Compile instructions

from developer command prompt for vs 2022
cl.exe /O2 /MT parsec.c
